		'title' => 'Marketing planned across the channels you actually use.',
		'eyebrow' => 'Market',
		'card' => 'Strategy, campaigns, and reporting that connect search, content, and paid media.',
		'intro' => 'Sovassa is a digital marketing service provider for search, content, social, and paid media planned as one system. A digital marketing agency, or a digital marketing company hired channel by channel, often leaves the page behind the campaign. Digital marketing services here can still be a single channel when that is the real brief.',
		'detail' => array(
			'The plan names the offer, the audience, and the page that should receive the visit. Channels without that page are not launched to fill a calendar. Follow-up is part of the design: an enquiry needs an owner, not only a form that stores a name.',
			'A month ends with a note about what changed, what did not, and the next decision. The work is judged on that decision, not on how many assets were produced. If your team will publish, we can plan and review. If you want execution, that is scoped as its own work.',
			'Education programs are one place this shows up: many courses, and a prospective student who cannot tell which one is theirs. More ads do not fix that. The course page has to exist first. Campaigns then land on that page, not on a list of every program.',
			'The first conversation names the offer, the person who should enquire, and who replies after the form. If those three are unclear, the useful work is the message and the page, not a new channel. A monthly note then says what changed, what stayed flat, and the one decision for the next month. Adding a channel because the calendar looks empty is a recommendation we will not make. Your team can publish while we plan and review, or execution can be scoped on its own.',
		),
