	'social-media-marketing' => array(
		'layout' => 'service', 'pillar' => 'market', 'wp_title' => 'Social Media Marketing', 'nav_label' => 'Social Media',
		'title' => 'Social presence with a point of view and a next step.',
		'eyebrow' => 'Market',
		'card' => 'Strategy, creative, community, and paid social when it earns a place.',
		'intro' => 'What is social media marketing, for a company rather than a textbook? It is a small set of platforms, a repeating point of view, and a next step that matches the website. Sovassa plans that presence, the creative, and the replies. Paid social is added only when a page is ready to receive it.',
		'detail' => array(
			'The first decision is which rooms are worth the team’s time. Two platforms run properly beat six accounts that go quiet. Content pillars come from the offer and the questions buyers already ask, so a month does not start from a blank post.',
			'Community needs a named owner and a rule for what the company will say in public. Sensitive replies stay with someone inside the business. Creative uses a small set of layouts. A bespoke asset is for a campaign, not for every Tuesday.',
			'When the company sells expertise, the useful version is a steady explanation of the offer, close enough to the website that sales can recognise it. It is not a second brand. Professional-services firms usually need fewer posts and a clearer next step, not a presence on every network.',
			'A month has a small set of themes, a layout the team can repeat, and a named owner for replies. Sensitive comments stay with someone inside the company. Paid promotion waits until a page can receive the visit and continue the same offer. We would rather keep two networks current than open accounts that go quiet. A calendar full of posts, with no destination and no one reading the replies, is the failure mode this engagement is meant to avoid.',
		),
		'industry' => 'industries/professional-services',
