	'google-ads' => array(
		'layout' => 'service', 'pillar' => 'market', 'wp_title' => 'Google Ads / PPC', 'nav_label' => 'Google Ads',
		'title' => 'Paid search that sends people to a page ready for them.',
		'eyebrow' => 'Market',
		'card' => 'Account structure, keywords, ads, tracking, and the landing pages they depend on.',
		'intro' => 'Google search ads work when the query, the ad, and the landing page describe the same offer. Sovassa manages that system: account structure, keywords, ads, and the tracking that tells a useful enquiry from noise. Spend does not grow to hide a page that is not ready.',
		'detail' => array(
			'The account is grouped by offer and intent, so a research query and a buying query do not share one budget by accident. Negative keywords and a conversion your team agrees is real come before any judgement of the campaign. You own the ad account. We work inside it.',
			'Landing pages are part of the engagement when the current site cannot continue the promise in the ad. We will pause a muddy setup rather than report it as success. A cost per lead is a range after we see the offer, not a guarantee in the first call.',
			'Ecommerce is a typical case. Ads for a collection only help when the shelf matches the ad. If merchandising and acquisition were planned apart, the first job is the page, then the queries that should reach it. We will not point spend at a homepage that does not continue the offer.',
			'A review looks at search terms, the ads people actually saw, and whether the enquiry was one your team wanted. Junk leads are called junk. Budget moves toward the offer that produced a real conversation, and away from queries that only look busy. Creative changes when the same ad has been ignored, not on a calendar. If the useful next step is a clearer page rather than a higher bid, that is the recommendation, even when it means spending less for a while.',
		),
